    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-A2-S1",
      "band": "A2",
      "topic_family": "travel",
      "text": "Passengers for Greenford should note that the 11:20 service is delayed by about fifteen minutes because of a signalling problem. It will still leave from Platform 2.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-A2-01",
        "LSN-A2-02"
      ],
      "speakers": "One speaker",
      "target_wpm": 138,
      "domain": "public",
      "word_count": 27,
      "est_duration_sec": 11.7,
      "speaker_count": 1,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-A2-S2",
      "band": "A2",
      "topic_family": "schedule",
      "text": "A: Can we move the team call to Friday? B: Friday morning is difficult for me, but I am free after three. A: Let us make it three thirty then.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-A2-03",
        "LSN-A2-04"
      ],
      "speakers": "Two speakers",
      "target_wpm": 138,
      "domain": "occupational",
      "word_count": 30,
      "est_duration_sec": 13.0,
      "speaker_count": 2,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-A2-S3",
      "band": "A2",
      "topic_family": "event",
      "text": "The outdoor film will begin at eight as planned. The cafe will close at seven thirty, so please buy food before then. If it rains, the film will move into the main hall.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-A2-05",
        "LSN-A2-06"
      ],
      "speakers": "One speaker",
      "target_wpm": 138,
      "domain": "public",
      "word_count": 33,
      "est_duration_sec": 14.3,
      "speaker_count": 1,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-B1-S1",
      "band": "B1",
      "topic_family": "service_change",
      "text": "A: I thought the new booking system was supposed to make things quicker. B: It does when you already know the service you need, but first-time users seem to spend longer choosing. A: So the problem is not the payment stage? B: Not really. Most delays happen before people reach it.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-B1-01",
        "LSN-B1-02"
      ],
      "speakers": "Two speakers",
      "target_wpm": 150,
      "domain": "public",
      "word_count": 51,
      "est_duration_sec": 20.4,
      "speaker_count": 2,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-B1-S2",
      "band": "B1",
      "topic_family": "presentation",
      "text": "When you prepare a short presentation, do not try to include everything you know. Decide on one main message and choose two or three examples that support it. If a detail is interesting but does not help that message, leave it out. You can always answer questions afterwards.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-B1-03",
        "LSN-B1-04"
      ],
      "speakers": "One speaker",
      "target_wpm": 150,
      "domain": "educational",
      "word_count": 48,
      "est_duration_sec": 19.2,
      "speaker_count": 1,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-B1-S3",
      "band": "B1",
      "topic_family": "volunteer",
      "text": "A: We need someone at the entrance from ten. B: I can do ten to twelve, but I have to leave after that. C: I am free from eleven, so I could take over at noon. A: Perfect. I will cover the first few minutes if traffic makes anyone late.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-B1-05",
        "LSN-B1-06"
      ],
      "speakers": "Three speakers",
      "target_wpm": 150,
      "domain": "public",
      "word_count": 50,
      "est_duration_sec": 20.0,
      "speaker_count": 3,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-B2-S1",
      "band": "B2",
      "topic_family": "meeting_format",
      "text": "A: I like the idea of shorter meetings, but sending every update in writing could create another problem. People may stop reading them. B: True. What if written updates are limited to three points, and the meeting is used only for decisions or questions? A: That sounds more realistic. It keeps the record without turning the inbox into a report archive.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-B2-01",
        "LSN-B2-02"
      ],
      "speakers": "Two speakers",
      "target_wpm": 156,
      "domain": "occupational",
      "word_count": 61,
      "est_duration_sec": 23.5,
      "speaker_count": 2,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-B2-S2",
      "band": "B2",
      "topic_family": "housing",
      "text": "A council is considering converting an unused office building into temporary housing. Supporters point out that the building is already connected to transport and basic services. Critics argue that the internal layout was never designed for long-term living. The council has therefore commissioned a feasibility study before making a final decision.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-B2-03",
        "LSN-B2-04"
      ],
      "speakers": "One speaker",
      "target_wpm": 156,
      "domain": "public",
      "word_count": 51,
      "est_duration_sec": 19.6,
      "speaker_count": 1,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-B2-S3",
      "band": "B2",
      "topic_family": "group_project",
      "text": "A: We divided the research by topic, which was efficient, but our final report sounds like three separate documents. B: Maybe we should agree on the argument first, then edit each section around it. C: I agree, though we should keep some differences in perspective rather than forcing every section to sound identical.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-B2-05",
        "LSN-B2-06"
      ],
      "speakers": "Three speakers",
      "target_wpm": 156,
      "domain": "educational",
      "word_count": 53,
      "est_duration_sec": 20.4,
      "speaker_count": 3,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-C1-S1",
      "band": "C1",
      "topic_family": "risk_communication",
      "text": "When organisations communicate risk, numbers can create an impression of precision that the underlying evidence does not justify. Saying that an event is \"unlikely\" may be vague, but giving a figure such as 8.3 percent is not automatically more honest if the model itself is highly uncertain. Good communication therefore needs two kinds of clarity: what the estimate currently is, and how much confidence we should place in it. The second is often harder to express because people mistake uncertainty for incompetence, even when uncertainty is an accurate feature of the evidence.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-C1-01",
        "LSN-C1-02"
      ],
      "speakers": "One speaker",
      "target_wpm": 162,
      "domain": "public",
      "word_count": 92,
      "est_duration_sec": 34.1,
      "speaker_count": 1,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-C1-S2",
      "band": "C1",
      "topic_family": "peer_feedback",
      "text": "A: The students said they wanted more detailed feedback, so we wrote much longer comments. B: Did that help? A: Not as much as we expected. Several students focused on correcting every small error and missed the two priorities we wanted them to work on. B: So perhaps more feedback is not the same as more useful feedback. A: Exactly. We are thinking of separating essential changes from optional suggestions next time.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-C1-03",
        "LSN-C1-04"
      ],
      "speakers": "Two speakers",
      "target_wpm": 162,
      "domain": "educational",
      "word_count": 72,
      "est_duration_sec": 26.7,
      "speaker_count": 2,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-C1-S3",
      "band": "C1",
      "topic_family": "implementation",
      "text": "A: The pilot worked well in the city office, so leadership wants to use the same process everywhere. B: That is encouraging, but the smaller sites do not have the same staffing. C: Could we keep the core steps and let each site decide how to organise them? A: That may be the safest way to scale it without pretending the contexts are identical.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-C1-05",
        "LSN-C1-06"
      ],
      "speakers": "Three speakers",
      "target_wpm": 162,
      "domain": "occupational",
      "word_count": 64,
      "est_duration_sec": 23.7,
      "speaker_count": 3,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-C2-S1",
      "band": "C2",
      "topic_family": "forecasting",
      "text": "Forecasts are often evaluated as though they were passive descriptions of a future that unfolds independently of them. In some settings that is a poor assumption. A warning about severe congestion may cause commuters to change their plans, preventing the congestion that was predicted. Calling the forecast \"wrong\" would then ignore the role it played in changing the outcome. The reverse is also possible: a confident demand forecast can encourage investment that helps create the demand. Evaluation therefore needs to ask not only whether a forecast matched what later happened, but how publishing it altered the system being forecast.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-C2-01",
        "LSN-C2-02"
      ],
      "speakers": "One speaker",
      "target_wpm": 166,
      "domain": "public",
      "word_count": 99,
      "est_duration_sec": 35.8,
      "speaker_count": 1,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-C2-S2",
      "band": "C2",
      "topic_family": "expertise",
      "text": "A: People often say that experts communicate badly because they use too much technical language. B: Sometimes, yes. But simplifying the vocabulary does not solve the deeper problem if the expert has not decided what the audience actually needs to understand. A: So the issue is selection as much as wording. B: Exactly. You can write in plain English and still give the wrong explanation if you choose the wrong distinctions.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-C2-03",
        "LSN-C2-04"
      ],
      "speakers": "Two speakers",
      "target_wpm": 166,
      "domain": "educational",
      "word_count": 71,
      "est_duration_sec": 25.7,
      "speaker_count": 2,
      "admin_only": true
    },
    {
      "stimulus_id": "LSN-C2-S3",
      "band": "C2",
      "topic_family": "heritage_decision",
      "text": "A: If we restore the hall exactly as it looked in 1920, visitors will see the original design more clearly. B: But the changes made in the 1960s are now part of its history too. C: Perhaps we should stop asking which period is \"the authentic one\" and explain why different choices preserve different kinds of evidence. A: That would make the decision more transparent, though less simple.",
      "item_ids": [
        "LSN-C2-05",
        "LSN-C2-06"
      ],
      "speakers": "Three speakers",
      "target_wpm": 166,
      "domain": "public",
      "word_count": 68,
      "est_duration_sec": 24.6,
      "speaker_count": 3,
      "admin_only": true
    }
